IMPORT prelude

-- Section 1: Purposes.
-- A purposes clause creates no rule, so this module carries it as quoted text and nothing consults it.
-- (Section 2, Commencement, states only dates and is encoded in vmu-time.)

§ `Section 1 -- Purposes (not operative)`

-- src:22 | 1 Purposes
-- src:23 | The main purposes of this Act are—
-- src:24 | (a) to provide for fees and penalties to be fixed by reference to fee units or penalty units that can be indexed annually by an amount to be fixed by the Treasurer;
-- src:25 | (b) to change certain penalties that are specified in monetary amounts in certain Acts to penalty units;
-- src:26 | (c) to change certain fees that are specified in monetary amounts in certain Acts to fee units;
-- src:27 | (d) to authorise the Governor in Council to make regulations—
-- src:28 | (i) converting references to fees and penalties in monetary amounts to equivalent fee units and penalty units;
-- src:29 | (ii) converting references to fee units and penalty units to equivalent fees and penalties in monetary amounts;
-- src:30 | (iii) converting existing references to fee units to equivalent fee units under this Act;
-- src:31 | (iv) converting existing references to the monetary value of fee units or penalty units to the equivalent value under this Act;
-- src:32 | (v) increasing fees that have remained in monetary amounts to fee units having regard to the indexation that would have applied if they were in fee units;
-- src:33 | (e) to change penalty units in the Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982 to monetary amounts;
-- src:34 | (f) to amend the Sentencing Act 1991 and the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994.
@ref s 1 (src:22-34)
`s 1 -- the main purposes of this Act, as the text prints them` MEANS
    LIST "The main purposes of this Act are—"
       , "(a) to provide for fees and penalties to be fixed by reference to fee units or penalty units that can be indexed annually by an amount to be fixed by the Treasurer;"
       , "(b) to change certain penalties that are specified in monetary amounts in certain Acts to penalty units;"
       , "(c) to change certain fees that are specified in monetary amounts in certain Acts to fee units;"
       , "(d) to authorise the Governor in Council to make regulations—"
       , "(i) converting references to fees and penalties in monetary amounts to equivalent fee units and penalty units;"
       , "(ii) converting references to fee units and penalty units to equivalent fees and penalties in monetary amounts;"
       , "(iii) converting existing references to fee units to equivalent fee units under this Act;"
       , "(iv) converting existing references to the monetary value of fee units or penalty units to the equivalent value under this Act;"
       , "(v) increasing fees that have remained in monetary amounts to fee units having regard to the indexation that would have applied if they were in fee units;"
       , "(e) to change penalty units in the Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982 to monetary amounts;"
       , "(f) to amend the Sentencing Act 1991 and the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994."
